        "created_at": "2013-03-15T02:19:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I am not sure I have seen this mentioned anywhere and wanted to clarify. When you flip a villian, what do you do with any left over damage? &nbsp;For example, Baron Blade is a at 2 HP on his A side. Chrono-Ranger hits him for 5. He loses the 2 HP and flips to side B, but what if anything happens to the 3 left over damage? &nbsp;</p><p>I had been playing it where it came off of the HP total on side B, meaning it would carry over. However, as I was thinking about it recently, I have started playing it just as if it was a normal target that was destroyed and a new target comes in to play to replace it. In this fashion, the extra damage would be wasted just as if you took out a normal target with excess damage.&nbsp;</p><p>Wondering what other people do and if there is an official ruling.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:37.964Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
